.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Node / workbench
node_modules/
.next/
# The deploy builds into .next.staging and renames it onto .next only after the
# build succeeds, so the live server never loses the directory it serves from.
# .next.previous is the outgoing build, held for the moment the rename takes.
# See build_next_staged in scripts/vps_apply.sh.
.next.staging/
.next.previous/
out/

# Data / runtime
*.log
data/
logs/
.tmp/
tmp/

# Docker volumes (if mounted locally)
infra/volumes/

# CodeGraph — per-checkout local symbol index (dev-velocity tooling, Phase 2).
# The .mcp.json + codegraph.json config IS committed; the index is not.
.codegraph/
.codegraph.db
codegraph.db

# Theia IDE (old PRD - ADR-014 removed)
ide/
.vps

# Playwright transient artifacts
/test-results/
workbench/control_plane/test-results/
# visual-review captures. Evidence for one review, never a committed baseline —
# a checked-in screenshot becomes a second source of truth about how the app
# looks, and it goes stale the first time anybody changes a token.
workbench/control_plane/ux-shots/

# Agent harness. ⚠️ NOT a blanket ignore any more (D29, 2026-08-10).
#
# `.claude/` holds the development philosophy in EXECUTABLE form — the
# supervisor-worker agent definitions, the /next-ticket command, and
# `plan-guard.mjs`, which is what refuses work_plan.md §6's owner-gated actions.
# While the whole directory was ignored, any checkout that was not this laptop —
# a cloud Claude instance, a fresh clone, a headless run, an agent worktree — ran
# with **no owner-gate enforcement and none of the review loop**. That is a
# safety control travelling by accident, so the harness is now tracked and only
# the genuinely local parts are ignored.
#
# Track: AGENTS.md · agents/ · commands/ · hooks/ · settings.json
# Ignore: everything below.
#
# ⚠️ Comments MUST be on their own line. `#` does not start a comment mid-line,
# so `foo/   # why` is a literal pattern ending in the comment text and matches
# nothing. The first draft of this block wrote it that way and committed the
# 2.3 MB skill bundle it says to ignore.
#
# per-machine permissions/overrides; may name local paths
.claude/settings.local.json
# ephemeral full checkouts made by parallel agents
.claude/worktrees/
# runtime state
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
# local observation logs
.claude/skill-observations/
# third-party skill bundles (tooling a developer installs, not project doctrine)
# ⚠️ `*`, not a trailing slash. Git does not descend into an ignored DIRECTORY,
# so a negation below would never be reached and the exception would look like a
# typo rather than failing loudly.
.claude/skills/*
# ...except the skills that ARE project doctrine and must travel with the repo,
# the same reason .claude/agents and .claude/commands are tracked (D29). Claude
# Code discovers skills HERE and not in .github/skills, so a doctrine skill kept
# out of this directory is a skill nobody loads.
!.claude/skills/ste/
# Vendored from github.com/dickwu/apple-design-skill @ d0bac1e (owner ask,
# 2026-08-31): the HIG design-review skill every checkout must load.
!.claude/skills/apple-design/
# Adopted from skills/upstream/anthropics/ @ 53048666 (owner ask, 2026-09-03).
# The mirror under skills/upstream/ is a REVIEW copy that nothing loads — Claude
# Code reads .claude/skills/ only. Adoption is this line, and nothing else.
# ⚠️ Three of the five carry a METORITE ADOPTION NOTE below their frontmatter,
# because their advice fights DESIGN_SYSTEM.md §0. A refresh drops that note.
# The adoption procedure lives in skills/upstream/README.md.
!.claude/skills/webapp-testing/
!.claude/skills/frontend-design/
!.claude/skills/skill-creator/
!.claude/skills/theme-factory/
!.claude/skills/brand-guidelines/
# Ours, not vendored: the visual-review rig. It is the gate DESIGN_SYSTEM.md §0
# asks for and the conformance suite cannot supply, so every checkout needs it.
# The STE linter DOES bind it — it is our prose.
!.claude/skills/visual-review/
skill-observations/

# Runtime caches / secrets / junk that must never be committed (foundation audit F2).
# .zoho_token_cache.json is regenerated at runtime by ingestion/sources/zoho/client.py.
*.pid
*.bak
*_dump.bak
*token_cache*.json
.zoho_token_cache.json

# Redis snapshot from a locally-run redis-server (dev/verification only)
dump.rdb
